\
Mbox Firmware Update Rev 20 OS X Read Me
\fs24 \
\
April, 2003\
\
\
Who Should Use This?\
\
Mbox users on OS X with older firmware.\
\
What Does this File Do?\
\
This software will update your Mbox firmware to version 20.\
\
This firmware version resolves the following issues:\
\
1. Fixes a problem with S/PDIF transfers from Mbox S/PDIF output to older S/PDIF devices at 48 kHz that could not lock to the S/PDIF clock from Mbox.\
\
2. Alleviates some cases where Mbox is not seen on the USB bus when plugged in or the computer is booted (USB light on Mbox fails to light).\
\
3. The input select lights on Channel 1 & 2 sometimes bounce around when selecting the input select switch.\
\
\
How Do I Use It?\
\
1. Download Mbox Firmware Rev 20 for Mac OS X from the Support/Downloads section at: www.digidesign.com/download\
\
2. Pro Tools 6.0 or higher for OS X must be already installed in order for the driver to recognize the Mbox.\
\
3. Quit the Pro Tools application if it is open.\
\
4. Plug the Mbox into your computer's USB port.\
\
5. Double-Click the application: Mbox Updater OSX.rev20\
\
6. Follow the on-screen instructions. You will be asked to plug and unplug the USB cable during the process.\
\
7. After you have completed your Firmware update, plug the USB cable back into the Mbox and the computer before launching Pro Tools. It is not necessary to restart.\
\
\
Regards,\
\
Digidesign Technical Support\
